.TH LUXAFOR-TRAY 1 "" "luxafor-status" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
luxafor-tray \- system tray icon showing the Luxafor status
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B luxafor-tray
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B luxafor-tray
shows a dot in the system tray with the color of the current status.
Its menu sets a status in one click, starts one of the timer shortcuts
(see
.B timer-shortcuts
in
.BR luxafor-toggle (1)),
opens
.BR luxafor-panel (1)
for any other duration (also with a middle-click on the icon), turns the
light off, opens the status configuration, or quits. While a timer runs, the time left is
shown next to the dot and at the top of the menu, with an entry to cancel it.
.PP
It follows changes made by
.BR luxafor-toggle (1)
from anywhere (launcher, keyboard shortcut, terminal) and reloads the
configuration when the file is saved.
.PP
It is started at login through
.IR /etc/xdg/autostart/luxafor-tray.desktop .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR luxafor-panel (1),
.BR luxafor-light (1),
.BR luxafor-toggle (1)
